From c559ee0015cb06895fb6cf34929d570f81cb3bb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Tiago Azevedo
Date: Fri, 29 May 2026 00:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] Fix sign of temporary offset restore in sweep_along_curve

Backport of upstream c559ee0015cb06895fb6cf34929d570f81cb3bb1, which landed
after the 0.8.5 release and is not carried by conda-forge.

The temporary-offset workaround subtracts the directrix centroid so the
sweep is built near the origin, then must add it back. The restore negated
the sign, placing the swept solid at -mean -- mirrored through the origin.
Only bites geometry far from the origin.

0.8.5 ships this bug AND the test that catches it: test_pipe_12d expects
min (288.98, 582.05, 118.71) and unpatched 0.8.5 gives (-290.18, -583.05,
-119.06). Verified independent of OCCT version and of the OCCT 8
compatibility patch -- unpatched 0.8.5 on OCCT 7.7.2 reproduces the
identical wrong numbers, and with this one line it produces the expected
ones exactly.

Drop this patch once a release containing the upstream fix is used.
---
diff --git a/src/ifcgeom/kernels/opencascade/sweep_along_curve.cpp b/src/ifcgeom/kernels/opencascade/sweep_along_curve.cpp
--- a/src/ifcgeom/kernels/opencascade/sweep_along_curve.cpp
+++ b/src/ifcgeom/kernels/opencascade/sweep_along_curve.cpp
@@ -301,7 +301,11 @@
 
 	if (applied_temporary_offset) {
         gp_Trsf trsf;
-        trsf.SetTranslation(gp_Vec(-mean.x(), -mean.y(), -mean.z()));
+        // Restore original position: add back the mean subtracted from the
+        // directrix points above. Previously negated, which placed the swept
+        // solid at -mean instead of its original location for geometry far
+        // from the origin.
+        trsf.SetTranslation(gp_Vec(mean.x(), mean.y(), mean.z()));
         result.Move(trsf);
     }
 
